                        ],
                        "form": "redoubling"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "8e6e6406-ccaa-4677-b609-3a48cf36c4d9",
                        "entry_id": "9c0fb14c-aa6b-34dd-802f-cbff1d07dc91",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "redoubled"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "e099a8ca-7a0b-49aa-ba28-b148369f6160",
                        "entry_id": "9c0fb14c-aa6b-34dd-802f-cbff1d07dc91",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "redoubled"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9f4386c6-b157-3d6c-b7b1-5380a4cf3875",
                        "entry_id": "9c0fb14c-aa6b-34dd-802f-cbff1d07dc91",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To double, especially to double again; to increase considerably; to multiply; to intensify."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "27410451-6064-4ac4-afe4-ba5f69aa9ca9",
                                "sense_id": "9f4386c6-b157-3d6c-b7b1-5380a4cf3875",
                                "text": "Having lost sight of our objectives, we redoubled our efforts."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a3e7e58-c8dc-4741-bbd0-035c70fcfa70",
                                "sense_id": "9f4386c6-b157-3d6c-b7b1-5380a4cf3875",
                                "text": "Every item of intelligence appeared to redouble the astonishment of the islanders, and they gazed at us with inquiring looks."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7f4e1e55-e67f-4e4d-a0ad-285db64ed3ce",
                                "sense_id": "9f4386c6-b157-3d6c-b7b1-5380a4cf3875",
                                "text": "The police redoubled their efforts to capture the thieves."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4eeb238d-837a-4e5d-b35d-420ccf0457cb",
                                "sense_id": "9f4386c6-b157-3d6c-b7b1-5380a4cf3875",
                                "text": "He heard the footsteps of his pursuers behind him, and redoubled his own pace. Once he got out of these by-ways he would be safe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a9912e2c-f9c6-4cf5-97bd-2df88973befc",
                                "sense_id": "9f4386c6-b157-3d6c-b7b1-5380a4cf3875",
                                "text": "With suggestions that inflation will rise above 15%, I have no doubt that today's trade union leaders will redouble their efforts to secure their members a good deal."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5cae7ef6-8f9e-3e0e-95ca-293db4f7f633",
                        "entry_id": "9c0fb14c-aa6b-34dd-802f-cbff1d07dc91",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To double an opponent's doubling bid."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "221722cc-786a-3372-ac38-3aba5fa14c07",
                        "entry_id": "9c0fb14c-aa6b-34dd-802f-cbff1d07dc91",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To become twice as big."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "215a78d7-a416-3c59-b471-0f57449f650a",
                        "entry_id": "9c0fb14c-aa6b-34dd-802f-cbff1d07dc91",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To double again what was reduced to a single state."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f37c4fd-3f28-4995-815b-f822eeafd368",
                                "sense_id": "215a78d7-a416-3c59-b471-0f57449f650a",
                                "text": "Like the Conservatives and Labour, the Lib Dems plan to extend Britain's rail network, reopen stations and redouble singled routes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
